---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import DiffViewer from '../../components/DiffViewer.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="Code / Text Diff Viewer" description="Compare two blocks of text or code line-by-line and see what changed.">
  <DiffViewer client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why a visual diff beats manual comparison</h2>
  <p>Spotting the difference between two similar blocks of text by eye is slow and error-prone, especially for long content — a line-by-line diff highlights exactly what changed, added, or was removed.</p>

  <h2>How to use this tool</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Paste the original text/code on one side.</li>
    <li>Paste the modified version on the other.</li>
    <li>Review the highlighted line-by-line differences.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Common Diff Viewer Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Comparing content with different line endings</strong> (Windows vs. Unix), which can cause every line to appear changed even when the visible content is identical.</li>
    <li><strong>Not accounting for whitespace-only differences</strong> that may not matter for your comparison but show up as changes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to Use This Diff Viewer</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Comparing two versions of a config file to spot what changed</li>
    <li>Checking the difference between two drafts of a document</li>
    <li>Reviewing what a formatter or auto-fix tool actually changed in a file</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Text Diff Viewer FAQ</h2>
  <p><strong>Does this work for any text, or just code?</strong> Any plain text works — code, config files, prose, or structured data like JSON.</p>
</ToolLayout>
